From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rust: link target artifacts with the sanitizers their C is
 compiled with

A crate that builds C, as libsqlite3-sys and aws-lc-sys do with cc-rs,
compiles it with TARGET_CFLAGS, and the C links into the target
artifact through the target's compiler. OpenWrt's package build gives
a link the sanitizer options of TARGET_CFLAGS (TARGET_LDFLAGS), but a
Rust package's link takes only RUSTFLAGS. With CONFIG_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION
holding -fsanitize=undefined -fsanitize-trap=undefined under LTO, the
link expanded the C's checks without -fsanitize-trap, as calls into
libubsan, which the musl toolchain does not have, and failed: thousands
of undefined __ubsan_handle_* in a binary linking SQLite and aws-lc.

Pass the sanitizer options of TARGET_CFLAGS to the target's link, as
link arguments. A build without sanitizers is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 lang/rust/rust-values.mk | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lang/rust/rust-values.mk b/lang/rust/rust-values.mk
--- a/lang/rust/rust-values.mk
+++ b/lang/rust/rust-values.mk
@@ -152,3 +152,10 @@
 CARGO_PKG_PROFILE:=$(if $(CONFIG_DEBUG),dev,release)
 
 CARGO_RUSTFLAGS+=-Clink-arg=-fuse-ld=$(TARGET_LINKER)
+
+# A sanitizer is a link option too: C that a crate's build compiles with
+# TARGET_CFLAGS, as cc-rs does, links into the target artifact, whose link adds
+# the sanitizer's runtime or, with -fsanitize-trap, leaves it out, and under LTO
+# expands the checks. The target's link takes the sanitizer options of
+# TARGET_CFLAGS, as OpenWrt's TARGET_LDFLAGS does.
+CARGO_RUSTFLAGS+=$(patsubst %,-Clink-arg=%,$(filter -fsanitize%,$(TARGET_CFLAGS)))
